---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { vonar } from '../../data/vonar';

// Steps follow "Installing in FL Studio" and "Quick guide" in the Vonar README.
const { installer, zip } = vonar;
---

<Base
  title="Install Vonar in FL Studio – step-by-step guide · Xami"
  description="How to install the free Vonar synth (VST3, Windows): download, the Windows SmartScreen warning, the installer, finding Vonar in FL Studio, presets and macros."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" class="guide wrap">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Installation guide</p>
      <h1 class="display">Install Vonar.<span class="muted">Step by step.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {`From download to your first sound in FL Studio. Vonar is a ${vonar.format} plugin for ${vonar.platform} (64-bit).`}
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2>Download the installer</h2>
          <p>
            Get <strong>{installer.fileName}</strong> ({installer.sizeLabel}). It comes straight from the{' '}
            <a href={vonar.releaseUrl}>GitHub release</a>.
          </p>
          <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href={installer.url}>Download {installer.fileName}</a></p>
          <details>
            <summary>Optional: check that the file is genuine</summary>
            <p>Open PowerShell in your Downloads folder and run:</p>
            <pre><code>Get-FileHash .\{installer.fileName} -Algorithm SHA256</code></pre>
            <p>The result must be exactly:</p>
            <pre><code class="hash">{installer.sha256}</code></pre>
            <p>
              Official downloads are only available from this site and the GitHub repository. Any other site is
              unofficial.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2 id="smartscreen">If Windows shows a blue “Windows protected your PC” window</h2>
          <p>
            This is Windows SmartScreen. It appears because the installer is not signed with a paid code-signing
            certificate, not because something is wrong with the file. Vonar is free and its full source code is{' '}
            <a href={vonar.repoUrl}>public on GitHub</a>.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <p class="callout-title">What to click</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Click <strong>More info</strong> (small text under the message).</li>
              <li>
                Check that the app name is <strong>{installer.fileName}</strong>. “Unknown publisher” is normal for
                an unsigned file.
              </li>
              <li>Click <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <p>Not sure? Check the SHA-256 in step 1 first. If it matches, the file is the one published here.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2>Run the installer</h2>
          <p>
            Follow the wizard: licence → install → finish. The plugin goes to{' '}
            <code>C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3\Vonar.vst3</code>, where every DAW looks for it. To remove it
            later, use <strong>Settings → Apps</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="aside">
            Prefer no installer? Download <a href={zip.url}>{zip.fileName}</a> and copy the whole{' '}
            <code>Vonar.vst3</code> folder to the same place.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2>Find Vonar in FL Studio</h2>
          <ol class="sub">
            <li>Open <strong>Options → Manage plugins</strong> and click <strong>Find installed plugins</strong>.</li>
            <li>
              Vonar appears under <strong>Generators</strong> (vendor: Vonar). Tick the star to show it in the
              instrument menu.
            </li>
            <li>In the <strong>Channel Rack</strong> click <strong>+</strong> and choose <strong>Vonar</strong>.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2>Pick a preset</h2>
          <p>
            Use the preset bar at the top of the Vonar window, not FL Studio's preset menu. Click the name to open
            the menu grouped by category, use the <strong>&lt; &gt;</strong> arrows to step through presets, or
            filter by category, mood and tag, and search.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
        <div class="body">
          <h2>Turn the macros</h2>
          <p>
            The four <strong>MACROS</strong> knobs at the bottom change the character of each preset. Drag a knob
            up or down, hold <strong>Shift</strong> for fine steps, and double-click to reset it. Your sound, preset
            name and macro labels are saved in the FL Studio project.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section class="more" aria-labelledby="more-title">
      <h2 id="more-title">Good to know</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your own presets</strong> (saved with <strong>SAVE</strong>) are JSON files in{' '}
          <code>%APPDATA%\Vonar\Presets</code>. After copying presets from another computer, choose{' '}
          <em>Rescan user presets</em> in the preset menu.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Coming from VOLT?</strong> Vonar was called VOLT during development. The installer removes the old{' '}
          <code>VOLT.vst3</code>, projects made with VOLT still open, and your presets are copied over.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Windows only.</strong> Vonar is a 64-bit (x64) VST3 plugin. There is no macOS or ARM64 build.</li>
        <li>More answers in the <a href={vonar.faqPath}>FAQ</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href={installer.url}>Download Vonar v{vonar.version}</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .guide {
    max-width: 840px;
    padding-top: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px);
    padding-bottom: 80px;
  }

  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 20px);
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: clamp(14px, 3vw, 24px);
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: 22px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 28px);
  }

  .num {
    flex: none;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--text);
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .body {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 6px 0 8px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 26px);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .body p,
  .body li,
  .more p,
  .more li {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  .body p,
  .more p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  a:not(.btn) {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Mono', Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--text);
    color: #fff;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  details {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 8px 0;
  }

  details[open] summary {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .callout {
    margin: 4px 0 12px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .body .callout-title {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    color: var(--eyebrow);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .callout ol,
  .sub {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .callout li + li,
  .sub li + li {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .aside {
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .more ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .more li + li {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
</style>
